Ooo!  Ooo!  I have!  It didn't seem to be too hard, except that the 
priestess (of Set, in this case) got really miffed afterwards.  Basically,
I came prepared for it.  It was in my current game, which is doing *very*
well (I'm now a 30th level mage on my way down Gehennom--gotta love those
wraiths), and I was on my way back after going to the Gnomish Mines to
get the luckstone I had heard about on this group.  On the way, I had
managed to acquire several potions of water, and I decided I wanted to 
turn them into holy water; since that temple of Set in the mine town was the
only altar I had seen so far, it was obvious that it needed to go.
So I located a scroll of create monster (one of the many such monsters carry
around these days), hefted my trusty +5 Mjollnir, and proceeded to summon
a blue dragon, right on top of the altar.  After slaying the loathsome
beastie, I sacrificed its carcass to Thoth, and the altar was converted.
No muss, no fuss.  Then the priestess got mad at me, and we fought back
and forth for a few rounds, during which time she summoned a bunch of 
insects to help her.  Once she was dead, I simply crushed them like...well,
insects. :)

Of course, I was pretty well-equipped and armored, since I was going back
through the Mines for the second time just to get something I had missed.
It would probably be tougher for someone who was either lower level, 
less well-outfitted, or both.  So this is probably not a good example.

Oh, as to why I summoned a blue dragon when they're immune to Mjolly's
special ability...I've decided to have some fun with this game by trying
to collect one of each type of dragon armor before I ascend (or die).  
So far I have blue, black, white, red, and gray (several sets).  Now I
just need green, yellow, and orange.  Sure I can't wear them all, but
it makes things more interesting to try.  Very much like the person
who plays the vegetarian Valkyrie. :)

